findings.body:
Reruns on the same head can block the PR. The review job's `cancel-in-progress: true` is keyed only on the PR number, so a run on the **same head** cancels the one in progress. Examples:
- the label is removed and re-added while a review is running (the header comment recommends this to get a fresh review);
- a `reopened` event arrives during a review;
- a `synchronize` run that already sees the label overlaps a `labeled` run.

The cancelled run leaves a cancelled "Review with Claude" check on the head commit. This PR's own ci.yml comment (lines 33-35) says that is exactly what made a cancelled "Test Suite" report as a failure. A failing check leaves the PR UNSTABLE, and PR Auto-Merge only merges CLEAN, even past the review cap. The same applies to the post job's group at line 134-135: two posts for the same head cancel each other.

Fix: include the head SHA in the group (e.g. `claude-review-${{ github.event.pull_request.number }}-${{ github.event.pull_request.head.sha }}`) and cancel only a run for an older head, or set `cancel-in-progress: false` for runs on the same head.

A failed review blocks the merge. If the Review step fails, the job fails and leaves a failing check on the head, so the PR is UNSTABLE and PR Auto-Merge won't merge it even at the review cap. Causes include:
- an expired or revoked `claude setup-token` OAuth token;
- an Anthropic outage or rate limit;
- a large PR hitting the 15-minute job timeout;
- the action returning no `structured_output`, after which the post step exits 1 on empty FINDINGS.

The PR stays stuck until someone pushes again, re-runs the job, or removes the label and pushes. While the token is broken, every labelled PR is blocked, which defeats Claude's role as a backup. The workflow already avoids failing on off-diff findings and on bot actors for exactly this reason.

Fix: add `continue-on-error: true` to this step (with a `::warning::`), and have the post job skip when `findings` is empty, or document that a review failure deliberately holds the PR.

Any push clears off-diff findings. The off-diff hold only looks at the latest Claude review **of the current head**, so it disappears on the next push whether or not anything was fixed. Example: Claude flags a bug outside the diff on head A. The next push B is one of:
- an unrelated commit or a merge from main;
- a push made while the label is off;
- a push by a bot actor, for which Claude Review skips.

Copilot then reviews B with no threads, `latestClaudeOfHead` is undefined, and the PR merges with Claude's finding never addressed (the test "ignores off-diff findings on an older head" encodes exactly this). Inline Claude threads, by contrast, keep holding across pushes until someone resolves them, so off-diff findings are much weaker than the docstring's "until the next push gets a fresh review" suggests.

Fix: judge by the latest marked Claude review across all commits (`claudeReviews.at(-1)`), and clear the hold only when a later Claude review has no off-diff marker, still bypassed at the cap.

`docs/PROCESS.md` is out of date. AGENTS.md says the merge process follows this document, but it still says PR Auto-Merge waits for "Copilot has reviewed its latest commit" and stops "after three Copilot review rounds". After this PR:
- a marked Claude review (from the `review:claude` label) also satisfies the gate;
- Claude's threads and its off-diff marker hold the merge;
- the cap counts Copilot's and Claude's rounds together.

Update this section (and mention the `review:claude` label and when to add it), so people and agents following PROCESS.md know why a PR is held or merged.
